.TH FFMPEG-ENCODE 1 "2026-10-06" "ffmpeg-encode" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ffmpeg-encode \- VAAPI HEVC/AV1 batch video encoder with curses TUI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ffmpeg-encode
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.P
.B ffmpeg-encode
.B \-i
\fIDIR\fR
[\fB\-i\fR \fIDIR\fR ...]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIDIR\fR]
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.P
.B ffmpeg-encode
.B \-\-input
\fIFILE\fR
[\fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.P
.B ffmpeg-encode\-av1
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ffmpeg-encode
is a wrapper around
.BR ffmpeg (1)
that re-encodes video with hardware-accelerated VAAPI
and shows a live
.BR curses (3)
interface for pausing, skipping and monitoring the queue.
It can process a whole directory tree (batch mode) or a single file, and in
batch mode several input directories can be given in one run.
.P
Two codecs are supported, both driven in constant-quality mode:
.B hevc
(default) selects
.BR hevc_vaapi ,
.B av1
selects
.BR av1_vaapi .
The
.B ffmpeg-encode\-av1
command is a thin wrapper that runs
.B ffmpeg-encode \-\-codec av1
with the same arguments.
.P
By default it reads from
.I /mnt/shared/Compressing
and writes to
.IR /mnt/shared/Handbraked ,
preserving relative paths under the output directory.
When several
.B \-i
directories are given, each file's path is preserved relative to the input
directory it was found under, so all inputs share the single output root.
.P
By default the original file is deleted after a successful encode, but
.B only
if the new file is smaller; if the encode came out larger the new file is
discarded and the original kept. Use
.B \-k
to keep both files unconditionally.
.P
With
.B \-\-vr
the encoder targets stereoscopic VR180/VR360 material. Such captures arrive
as a single, heavily pre-compressed side-by-side HEVC frame, so the normal
quality default can re-encode larger than the source and be discarded. VR
mode selects a more conservative quality default, writes its outputs under a
.B VR
subdirectory of the output root (for example
.IR /mnt/shared/Handbraked/VR ),
and, after a successful encode, refuses any output whose pixel dimensions
differ from the source (the job fails and the file is removed). It never
rescales, crops or reduces the frame, and an explicit
.B \-q
still overrides the default.
.P
The TUI shows a running percentage, frames per second, a smoothed encoding
speed multiplier and an estimated time remaining for the current file, the
per-file size result in the queue, and elapsed / queued counters in the
header. When the run ends, a summary reports how many files were done,
failed, skipped or kept, and the total space saved or gained.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-i " DIR"
Input directory for batch mode. May be repeated to encode several
directories in one run. Default:
.IR /mnt/shared/Compressing .
.TP
.BI \-o " DIR"
Output directory for batch mode. Default:
.IR /mnt/shared/Handbraked .
Relative paths under the input directory are preserved under this root. With
several
.B \-i
directories, the relative path is taken from whichever input directory the
file was found under; the output root is still single. With
.B \-\-vr
the files are placed one level deeper, under a
.B VR
subdirectory of this root.
.TP
.BI \-\-input " FILE"
Encode a single input file instead of scanning a directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " FILE"
Output path for single-file mode. If omitted, the name is derived from the
input path relative to the input directory and placed under the output
directory (for example
.IR /mnt/shared/Handbraked/movie.mkv ).
The extension is always forced to
.BR .mkv
even if another extension is given.
.TP
.BI \-\-codec " CODEC"
Video codec:
.B hevc
(default) or
.BR av1 .
The two codecs use different quality scales, so the default and meaning of
.B \-q
change with this option.
.TP
.BI \-p " PRESET"
Speed preset:
.BR speed ,
.BR balanced " (default), or " quality .
VAAPI exposes no quality preset, so this only sets
.BR \-async_depth
(8, 4 and 2 respectively); a larger value means more parallelism and a
faster encode with no effect on output quality.
.TP
.BI \-q " QP"
Constant-quality target. Lower means higher quality and larger files. The
valid range depends on the codec: HEVC 0\-51 (default 27), AV1 0\-255
(default 97). Out-of-range values are clamped.
.TP
.BI \-j " N"
.TP
.BI \-\-jobs " N"
Encode up to
.I N
files in parallel (default:
.BR 1 ).
Useful for batches of many small files where per-process ffmpeg / VAAPI
startup would otherwise dominate; a value of 2 or 3 is a good fit for a
VCN-class GPU.
.TP
.B \-n
Dry run. List the files that would be encoded and exit; no encoding or
deletion is performed.
.TP
.BI \-k ", " \-\-keep
Keep both the original and the encoded file. This is the opt-out from the
default behaviour of deleting the original, and it also keeps the encoded
file even when it is larger than the original.
.TP
.B \-\-vr
VR mode for stereoscopic VR180/VR360 captures. Sets the quality default to
HEVC
.B \-qp
30, or AV1
.B \-global_quality
130, writes outputs under a
.B VR
subdirectory of the output root, and verifies after encoding that the output
keeps the source's exact width and height; if it does not, the job is reported
as failed and the output removed. The encoder never downscales or crops in
this mode. An explicit
.B \-q
overrides the VR quality default.
.TP
.B \-h
Show a short help message and exit.
.SH BEHAVIOUR
.SS Encoding
.IP \(bu 2
Constant-quality mode:
.B hevc_vaapi
with
.B \-b:v 0 \-qp
.IR Q ,
or
.B av1_vaapi
with
.B \-rc_mode CQP \-global_quality
.IR Q
.IP \(bu 2
Decoding uses
.B \-hwaccel vaapi \-hwaccel_output_format vaapi
on an auto-detected device: the first
.I /dev/dri/renderD*
node, otherwise the first
.IR /dev/dri/card* ,
otherwise
.IR /dev/dri/renderD128
.IP \(bu 2
If VAAPI decoding cannot be initialised for a stream (for example a
malformed 4K SPS), the file is retried once with software decoding followed
by
.BR format=nv12,hwupload ;
the GPU still encodes
.IP \(bu 2
Audio streams are
.B copied
(not re-encoded)
.IP \(bu 2
If copying the audio makes the Matroska muxer fail (for example a corrupt
ADTS AAC lead-in in an MPEG-TS capture that ffmpeg cannot parse), the file
is retried once with the audio re-encoded as AAC at 160 kbit/s
.IP \(bu 2
Only video and audio are mapped (\fB\-map 0:v? \-map 0:a?\fR); subtitles
are skipped to avoid failures on some broadcast sources (e.g. DVB/teletext on
.BR .ts )
.IP \(bu 2
Existing output files are overwritten (\fB\-y\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
All outputs use the
.B .mkv
(Matroska) container, regardless of the input extension
.SS Deletion policy
After a successful encode the original is deleted
.B only
when the encoded file is smaller. If the encoded file is the same size or
larger, it is removed and the original is kept (the job is reported as
.IR kept ).
Passing
.B \-k
keeps both files in all cases. Files that are cancelled or quit are left
alone and the original is never removed.
.SS VR mode
Stereoscopic VR is delivered as one side-by-side frame (for example
5760x2880 HEVC at roughly 7.5 Mbit/s, that is two 2880x2880 fisheye eyes).
The platform has already compressed it heavily, so re-encoding at the normal
default can grow the file and be discarded as
.IR kept .
.B \-\-vr
raises the quality target to the conservative end that still produces a real
saving (HEVC QP 30, AV1 CQ 130) and, because VR viewers magnify any
resolution loss, fails any encode whose output dimensions differ from the
input. Colour range is preserved: full-range
.B yuvj420p
captures stay full-range through both the hardware and the software-decode
paths.
.P
VR outputs are kept separate from the normal encode tree: they are written
under a
.B VR
subdirectory of the output root (
.I /mnt/shared/Handbraked/VR
by default), with each input's relative path mirrored beneath it. An explicit
single-file
.B \-\-output
still wins over this placement.
.SS Batch discovery
In batch mode, files are found recursively under each input directory with
extensions (case-insensitive):
.BR mkv ", " mp4 ", " avi ", " mov ", " webm ", " ts ", " mts ", " webp .
.P
With several
.B \-i
directories the queues are processed
.IR blocked :
all files from the first directory (sorted) are queued before the second,
and so on, in the order the
.B \-i
flags are given. Overlapping directories are de-duplicated.
.SS Requirements
.IP \(bu 2
.B ffmpeg
built with VAAPI support
.IP \(bu 2
.B vainfo
available (from
.BR libva-utils )
.IP \(bu 2
.B ffprobe
(for duration / progress)
.IP \(bu 2
A terminal of at least 60 columns by 10 rows for the full interface
.SH EXAMPLES
Encode everything under the default directories:
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode
.EE
.P
Custom directories and a speed preset:
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode \-i ~/Videos/raw \-o ~/Videos/encoded \-p quality
.EE
.P
Two input directories into one output root (first directory is encoded first):
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode \-i ~/Videos/raw \-i /mnt/archive \-o ~/Videos/encoded
.EE
.P
Encode to AV1 instead of HEVC:
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode \-\-codec av1 \-q 110
.EE
.P
The same thing through the wrapper, which defaults to AV1:
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode-av1 \-i ~/Videos/raw
.EE
.P
Single file with an explicit output path:
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode \-\-input video.mkv \-\-output video-hevc.mkv \-p speed
.EE
.P
List what would be encoded without running it:
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode \-n \-i ~/Videos/raw \-o ~/Videos/encoded
.EE
.P
Tighter HEVC quality (lower QP):
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode \-q 24
.EE
.P
Encode a stereoscopic VR capture with the conservative VR defaults (output
goes to
.IR /mnt/shared/Handbraked/VR/vr180.mkv ):
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode \-\-vr \-\-input vr180.ts
.EE
.P
VR batch run into a custom split tree (outputs land in
.IR /mnt/shared/Other/VR ):
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode \-\-vr \-i /mnt/shared/Compressing \-o /mnt/shared/Other
.EE
.P
Encode a batch of small files with three parallel jobs:
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode \-i ~/Videos/raw \-o ~/Videos/encoded \-j 3
.EE
.P
Keep both the original and the encoded file:
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode \-k
.EE
.SH INTERACTIVE KEYS
.TP
.B p
Pause / resume encoding (sends
.B SIGSTOP
/
.B SIGCONT
to the running ffmpeg processes).
.TP
.B r
Resume encoding (alias for toggling pause off).
.TP
.B s
Skip the file(s) currently encoding: a partial output is removed and the
original is left untouched.
.TP
.B a
Add a file to the queue with an inline editor (Escape cancels).
.TP
.B A
Re-scan the input directories and queue any files not already present.
.TP
.B Up / Down, j / k
Scroll the queue list one line.
.TP
.B Page Up / Page Down
Scroll the queue list by half a page.
.TP
.B Home / End
Jump to the top / bottom of the queue.
.TP
.B f
Re-enable auto-follow, keeping the currently encoding file centred.
.TP
.B q
Quit. Any in-progress encodes are cancelled: their partial output is removed
and the original files are left untouched. Ctrl+C behaves the same.
.P
Scrolling with the arrow keys turns off auto-follow so the queue stops
jumping around; note that a terminal only repaints the focused tab, so an
unfocused tab may appear frozen until you switch back to it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The run completed and the TUI was closed, or a dry run finished. Note that
individual encode failures do not change the exit status; they are reported
in the summary.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid usage detected after parsing:
.B \-\-jobs
less than 1, a single input file that does not exist, or VAAPI not available.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line parsing error (unknown option, bad choice for
.B \-\-codec
or
.BR \-p ,
non-integer
.BR \-q ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /mnt/shared/Compressing
Default input directory (batch mode).
.TP
.I /mnt/shared/Handbraked
Default output directory (batch mode).
.TP
.I /mnt/shared/Handbraked/VR
Default output directory for
.B \-\-vr
batch mode.
.TP
.I /dev/dri/renderD128
Fallback VAAPI device when no node is auto-detected.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR ffprobe (1),
.BR vainfo (1),
.BR ffmpeg-encode-av1 (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use with VAAPI on AMD RDNA4 (RX 9070 class).
